WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.119
You already have immutable logs.

00:00:03.219 --> 00:00:05.538
CloudTrail integrity validation.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:06.538
Object Lock.

00:00:06.638 --> 00:00:10.044
But that only proves the record wasn't touched.

00:00:10.144 --> 00:00:11.380
Not that it's complete.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.108
EPI records the application layer.

00:00:15.208 --> 00:00:19.906
The prompt, the answer, the tool call, the policy decision.

00:00:20.006 --> 00:00:23.390
Hash chained, redacted, signed into one file.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.605
It answers three questions.

00:00:26.705 --> 00:00:28.583
Were the bytes altered.

00:00:28.683 --> 00:00:30.725
Is the signing key yours.

00:00:30.825 --> 00:00:32.948
Did the run follow policy.

00:00:33.048 --> 00:00:36.160
Change one byte, and the seal fails closed.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.479
The file is HTML and a ZIP.

00:00:39.579 --> 00:00:43.897
Open it in a browser, no account, no AWS console.

00:00:43.997 --> 00:00:49.260
Or witness only the hash, and keep the payload in your bucket.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.521
Don't argue with auditors.

00:00:52.621 --> 00:00:53.942
Hand them a file.

00:00:54.042 --> 00:00:57.461
Your immutable logs can stay where they are.

00:00:57.561 --> 00:00:58.494
Open source.

00:00:58.594 --> 00:00:58.660
M I T.
